  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Nucleus A decays into nucleus B as shown in the equation:</p>\n<p>A <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\rightarrow\"></span> B + 2<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha\"></span> + 4<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\beta^{-}\"></span></p>\n<p>Which of the following statements is <strong>not true</strong> about A and B?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">B is an isotope of A.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">The nucleon number of B is smaller than the nucleon number of A.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">B has the same number of protons as A.</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">B has the same number of neutrons as A.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
